        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਪਸਾਰਨਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਪਸਾਰਨਾ — pasārnā — \"to stretch out (arms or legs)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਵੇਰੇ ਮੈਂ ਮੰਜੇ ਉੱਤੇ ਲੱਤਾਂ ਪਸਾਰਦਾ ਹਾਂ। savere maiṁ manje utte lattāṁ pasārdā hāṁ. In the morning I stretch out my legs on the cot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਲੱਤਾਂ ਪਸਾਰੀਆਂ, maiṁ lattāṁ pasārīāṁ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਪਸਾਰਨਾ (pasārnā) is inherited from Sanskrit prasārayati, \"stretches out, extends\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi pasārṇā, \"to stretch out\" (CDIAL 8838). CDIAL adds that the Punjabi form may have been taken from the central languages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what you do."
